{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Therefore I weep.</b> Each and every man of Moab says:" "<b>vine of Sibmah.</b> A place name, and it lacks [the letter] vav." "<b>Your shoots.</b> A foreign word, for the yod is in place of the vav, and the vav is in place of the heh as a mater lectionis, and it is a foreign word. The kaf [is used] in addressing Heshbon, and it is the great district of Moab." "<b>your summer fruit.</b> The fruit of summer." "<b>Hedad.</b> This word is spoken by those who trample and tread. And behold, the fruit is destroyed and the harvest while it is still moist."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {2 "The Hebrew אריוך ('aryokh) is glossed as a foreign word; Ibn Ezra analyzes its morphology by letter substitution."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:03.201035193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}